WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.950
Imagine it is seven on Monday,
July second, twenty twelve,

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:07.630
and we need the hour beginning at eight.

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:11.550
The calendar and a previously
fitted model are available.

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:14.470
The observed count for that hour is not.

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:19.400
Our saved hour and working day group
returns three hundred and forty nine point

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:21.690
five zero rentals per hour.

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:27.490
The final question is how this already
chosen function behaves on later hours.

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:33.050
We must settle the function and reporting
rules before opening those later outcomes,

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:36.950
otherwise the assessment becomes
another development comparison.

00:00:39.358 --> 00:00:41.908
The models were fitted on twenty eleven.

00:00:42.418 --> 00:00:47.158
January through June twenty twelve
supplied the validation comparison that

00:00:47.158 --> 00:00:49.088
selected the raw group predictor.

00:00:49.718 --> 00:00:51.488
We retain those exact parameters,

00:00:51.938 --> 00:00:56.648
including seven existing representative
models and their chosen output policies.

00:00:57.278 --> 00:01:00.728
There is no final period
refit or new seed search.

00:01:01.318 --> 00:01:03.448
Tree families retain seed seventeen,

00:01:03.858 --> 00:01:08.028
the first declared seed, rather than
a seed chosen for its final score.

00:01:08.838 --> 00:01:12.278
A train plus validation refit could
have been declared beforehand,

00:01:12.278 --> 00:01:14.988
but would produce a different function.

00:01:15.558 --> 00:01:18.318
This assessment measures the
original historical fits,

00:01:18.318 --> 00:01:20.728
with that narrower claim explicit.

00:01:23.025 --> 00:01:27.935
Before accessing final outcomes,
the protocol binds model bytes,

00:01:28.045 --> 00:01:29.615
training fitted transforms,

00:01:30.085 --> 00:01:33.235
feature order, output policy and seeds.

00:01:33.505 --> 00:01:37.935
It also binds dataset membership,
source and dependency identities,

00:01:38.425 --> 00:01:39.115
metrics,

00:01:39.605 --> 00:01:40.315
counted slices

00:01:40.685 --> 00:01:42.335
and three example times.

00:01:42.705 --> 00:01:46.365
Every saved function first
reproduces its four thousand,

00:01:46.365 --> 00:01:50.415
three hundred and fifty seven
retained validation forecasts.

00:01:51.365 --> 00:01:54.425
The freeze was saved at
three ten thirty seven UTC,

00:01:54.425 --> 00:01:58.415
before the final run began
at three ten forty four.

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:03.995
The source receipt includes actual
file hashes alongside the Git parent.

00:02:04.485 --> 00:02:08.775
A commit name alone would not
describe newly changed executing code.

00:02:10.858 --> 00:02:13.828
The execution order is
visible in the code.

00:02:14.518 --> 00:02:17.588
First verify the frozen
protocol and saved models.

00:02:18.218 --> 00:02:21.038
Next predict from target
free final features,

00:02:21.038 --> 00:02:23.488
and durably write every forecast.

00:02:24.198 --> 00:02:29.078
Only afterward save the matching label
access receipt and join observed targets

00:02:29.078 --> 00:02:30.528
from the raw source.

00:02:31.118 --> 00:02:35.208
The join checks protocol and
forecast hashes, record identity,

00:02:35.698 --> 00:02:38.588
time, calendar and the raw source digest.

00:02:39.398 --> 00:02:43.648
The normal development loader still
rejects test labels before opening files.

00:02:44.178 --> 00:02:48.558
Separate guarded access preserves that
development boundary rather than adding a

00:02:48.558 --> 00:02:51.148
convenient test option
to every model study.

00:02:53.333 --> 00:02:54.883
Change a protocol hash,

00:02:55.353 --> 00:02:59.943
model bytes or raw source and the
relevant check rejects the assessment.

00:03:00.533 --> 00:03:05.133
Reordering an identity also fails rather
than pairing a prediction with another

00:03:05.133 --> 00:03:05.783
hour.

00:03:06.473 --> 00:03:11.203
Synthetic checks exercise these cases
without consuming new real targets.

00:03:12.193 --> 00:03:15.463
A valid but inaccurate
forecast belongs in the result;

00:03:15.793 --> 00:03:18.303
it is different from broken
provenance or alignment.

00:03:18.913 --> 00:03:20.973
Checksums establish byte identity,

00:03:20.973 --> 00:03:25.783
while inspected code and execution
receipts explain meaning and order.

00:03:26.173 --> 00:03:29.963
They do not prove the chosen model
is scientifically appropriate.

00:03:30.393 --> 00:03:31.743
On repeated invocation,

00:03:32.273 --> 00:03:36.563
the example shows the existing assessment
instead of silently replacing it.

00:03:38.608 --> 00:03:42.618
Suppose the final table motivates
a different model choice.

00:03:43.008 --> 00:03:47.338
We can keep the original fixed assessment
and report exactly what it found.

00:03:47.728 --> 00:03:50.618
The next choice is now
informed by this test.

00:03:50.988 --> 00:03:54.858
That can be useful development,
provided its history stays visible.

00:03:55.588 --> 00:04:00.388
A new independent quality claim needs
new held out evidence for the revised

00:04:00.388 --> 00:04:01.158
procedure.

00:04:01.748 --> 00:04:06.628
Randomly splitting these already inspected
outcomes again does not restore their

00:04:06.628 --> 00:04:07.618
original independence.

00:04:08.248 --> 00:04:11.538
The point of freezing is to
preserve the meaning of the result,

00:04:11.728 --> 00:04:13.378
including a disappointing one,

00:04:13.468 --> 00:04:17.098
rather than guarantee that the
original choice will always win.

